  "notes": "Prices in USD per 1M tokens, standard (non-batch) API tier. Tiered-price models record the base (lowest) tier with the higher tier in the model's note field. Retired models excluded; deprecated-but-available models included. Collected Monday on schedule. Tracked scope follows the set established on 2026-07-16 so week-over-week deltas stay meaningful: provider pages also list older or non-text models (OpenAI gpt-5.2 and earlier, Mistral Mixtral/NeMo/Ministral/Voxtral, Google image, embedding, TTS, video, and robotics models) that were outside scope then and remain outside it now. The tracked set holds at 43 rows; no model entered or left it. One price move, and it is a large one: OpenAI cut gpt-5.6-sol from $5.00/$30.00 to $4.00/$20.00 (cache read $0.50 to $0.40) — input -20%, output -33.3%. The page marks this as promotional and states it is available at least through 2026-11-21, so this is a dated cut rather than a new standard price. The other two 5.6 models, terra and luna, did not move. gpt-5.6-sol also now shows a separate long-context tier at $8.00/$30.00 (cache read $0.80), recorded in the model's note; OpenAI previously published flat per-model rates with no long-context tier, so this is the first tiered OpenAI row in the series. Still observed and still out of the rows, unchanged from 2026-08-17: Mistral's resale of Z.ai GLM 5.2 (zai-glm-5-2 on the pricing page, z-ai-glm-5-2 in the models overview) at $1.40/$4.40 with cached input $0.14, and Ministral 3 in three sizes. Both sit outside the scope fixed on 2026-07-16. Whether a third-party model resold on a tracked provider's API belongs in this series is a scope question for 기웅, not one to settle inside a collection run. New this week and also out of scope: DeepSeek shipped deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp at the same rates as v4-flash ($0.22/$0.66 off-peak, cache hit $0.007), excluded as a non-text model. Two forward signals carried from last week still stand on the pages: Anthropic's cancellation of the 2026-09-01 Sonnet 5 increase, and the 2026-12-31 promotional expiry on gemini-3.7-flash and gemini-3.6-flash. Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview and Gemini 3 Flash Preview were re-verified at unchanged rates after a first read of the page omitted them.",
